(2257183, 306768, 47415, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments, I didn''t think this would do this well. My husband is going to get new boots!</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments, I didn''t think this would do this well. My husband is going to get new boots!', '2006-03-25 03:16:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2257297, 305685, 50935, '<td valign="top">Thanks Everyone for all your wonderful comments.</td>', 'Thanks Everyone for all your wonderful comments.', '2006-03-25 07:15:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2258061, 306636, 5112, '<td valign="top">She''s a wondeful model.  Her face has a lot of character, and yet it is "model beautiful".<br/> <br/>I like this image very much.  I like the repeating lines: her silhouette repeated in the line of the hair over the eye; the back of the head repeated in the shoulders and hinted at with the top of her hips.  I also very much like the brown/black colour combination, the colours suit this girl beautifully.  I like the centred subject placement in this case - it works.  I like it that the model is not neatimaged to death, if there''s any noise reduction, it''s very subtle; I find the slight mottling in the skin of the arm very "human", goes well with the "without" title.<br/> <br/>One thing I wonder about is the silver insteps of the shoes - they don''t quite go along with the image, then again, if the insteps were black or white or gold maybe it would be too homogeneous.<br/> <br/>As far as DPC and scores goes, I imagine the reason it didn''t score higher is that the connection to footware is not "in your face".<br/> <br/>Cheers!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-03-25 15:54:28.</i></td>', 'She''s a wondeful model.  Her face has a lot of character, and yet it is "model beautiful". I like this image very much.  I like the repeating lines: her silhouette repeated in the line of the hair over the eye; the back of the head repeated in the shoulders and hinted at with the top of her hips.  I also very much like the brown/black colour combination, the colours suit this girl beautifully.  I like the centred subject placement in this case - it works.  I like it that the model is not neatimaged to death, if there''s any noise reduction, it''s very subtle; I find the slight mottling in the skin of the arm very "human", goes well with the "without" title. One thing I wonder about is the silver insteps of the shoes - they don''t quite go along with the image, then again, if the insteps were black or white or gold maybe it would be too homogeneous. As far as DPC and scores goes, I imagine the reason it didn''t score higher is that the connection to footware is not "in your face". Cheers!', '2006-03-25 15:11:06.000000', '2006-03-25 15:54:28.000000', 0),
(2258197, 306636, 5728, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ursula:</b></div><hr/><i> As far as DPC and scores goes, I imagine the reason it didn''t score higher is that the connection to footware is not "in your face".<br/>Cheers! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well to tell the truth I didn''t shoot this for the footwear challenge. We had a shooting on Saturday with some models and when I was looking through what we had shot I saw the shoes and just decided to enter it into the footwear challenge. I knew it wouldn''t be a top contender because as you say and as many have written here, the shoes are not the main subject in the image.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the comments everyone.</td>', 'Originally posted by ursula: As far as DPC and scores goes, I imagine the reason it didn''t score higher is that the connection to footware is not "in your face".Cheers!   Well to tell the truth I didn''t shoot this for the footwear challenge. We had a shooting on Saturday with some models and when I was looking through what we had shot I saw the shoes and just decided to enter it into the footwear challenge. I knew it wouldn''t be a top contender because as you say and as many have written here, the shoes are not the main subject in the image. Thanks for the comments everyone.', '2006-03-25 16:27:42.000000', NULL, 0),
