(2349302, 306952, 18090, '<td valign="top">Gosh, and the thing I was most unhappy with was the fact that I mis-spelled "inspector"...</td>', 'Gosh, and the thing I was most unhappy with was the fact that I mis-spelled "inspector"...', '2006-04-27 01:08:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2358421, 306790, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is sort of a transitional image for you, in your small portfolio. I look at the dates on your various entries, and I see such rapid improvement! I''m sure by now you''re aware how relatively unsophisticated the lighting is in this shot, and wish you could do it again. I''d make particular note that the pure black surround is not an ideal one for this subject, and that you have a vague "glare" on the box itself that is hurting you. That''s the wax overlay on the cardboard carton, I believe. Some sort of coating anyway. It is possible that a polarizing filter would solve that problem; they work to some degree even with artifical light.</td>', 'This is sort of a transitional image for you, in your small portfolio. I look at the dates on your various entries, and I see such rapid improvement! I''m sure by now you''re aware how relatively unsophisticated the lighting is in this shot, and wish you could do it again. I''d make particular note that the pure black surround is not an ideal one for this subject, and that you have a vague "glare" on the box itself that is hurting you. That''s the wax overlay on the cardboard carton, I believe. Some sort of coating anyway. It is possible that a polarizing filter would solve that problem; they work to some degree even with artifical light.', '2006-04-29 16:03:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2390874, 305737, 48228, '<td valign="top">Great close-up, and really would have liked this to have gained a much higher position in the challenge.....</td>', 'Great close-up, and really would have liked this to have gained a much higher position in the challenge.....', '2006-05-07 20:59:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2396624, 306929, 42125, '<td valign="top">Comment from a member of your own commenting club :-)<br/>Nice idea to hang your shoes up like this.<br/>What is good in this picture?:<br/>1. Focus is ok<br/>2. Nice colours<br/>What could be better?:<br/>1. Looks as there is a bit to much contrast<br/>2. The "faces" are a bit dark so at first sight you don''t see what it is you are looking at.<br/>3. The clouds are a bit blown up, to white. So I can see the trouble you are in, shoes to dark and clouds to bright and you have to apply the same to everything in the picture. In some editing programs you can apply brightness differenely to midtones and other without violating "Basic editing" rules.<br/>Hope this helps something.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-10 20:27:21.</i></td>', 'Comment from a member of your own commenting club :-)Nice idea to hang your shoes up like this.What is good in this picture?:1. Focus is ok2. Nice coloursWhat could be better?:1. Looks as there is a bit to much contrast2. The "faces" are a bit dark so at first sight you don''t see what it is you are looking at.3. The clouds are a bit blown up, to white. So I can see the trouble you are in, shoes to dark and clouds to bright and you have to apply the same to everything in the picture. In some editing programs you can apply brightness differenely to midtones and other without violating "Basic editing" rules.Hope this helps something.', '2006-05-09 10:23:06.000000', '2006-05-10 21:27:21.000000', 0),
